course: dictionary
lesson: 4048
title: One word, many meanings: general
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. The word general is a good example. «A general rule» means a rule that works for most things, not just one case. «A general idea» means the main idea, without all the details.
explain: Look at the words around general. In «general knowledge» and «the general public», general means for everyone or about many different things. In «a general in the army», it names a very high-ranking officer who leads soldiers. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Phrases help too. «In general» means usually or overall, and «as a general rule» means most of the time, though not always. When you are unsure, swap in a meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: General can describe things, as in «a general rule» or «general knowledge».
fact: A general is a noun: a very high-ranking officer in an army.
fact: «In general» means usually or overall.
fact: «As a general rule» means most of the time, but there can be exceptions.
fact: A GP is a general practitioner, a family doctor who knows a little about many health problems.
exercise: «Rubbish goes in the right bin: recycling, compost or general waste.» In this sentence, general waste means | *Rubbish that does not go in the special bins | Rubbish that is very old | Rubbish that is only glass | Rubbish that only soldiers make
exercise: «In maths, a general rule works for all numbers.» What does general mean here? | Made of soldiers | Only about one number | *For all cases, not just one particular case | Very loud
exercise: Find the word that means a high-ranking army officer in this sentence: «The general led the army across the river.» | army | *general | river | across
test: Mia says, «In general, I like rainy days.» What does in general mean here? | Never, not at all | Very loudly | Only on today | *Usually, overall
test: «General knowledge» means | Facts about only one topic, like cats | *Facts about many different topics | Secret facts known by one person | Knowing how to drive a car
exam: Which meaning of general fits «the general public»? | *Ordinary people, everyone in the country | Only one special person | A very high-ranking army officer | Not detailed, only the main idea
